\section*{Question 2}

Let \(f\) and \(g\) be the functions given by \(f(x)=2 x(1-x)\) and \(g(x)=3(x-1) \sqrt{x}\) for \(0 \leq x \leq 1\). The graphs of \(f\) and \(g\) are shown in the figure above.
\begin{itemize}
\item[(a)] Find the area of the shaded region enclosed by the graphs of \(f\) and \(g\).
\item[(b)] Find the volume of the solid generated when the shaded region enclosed by the graphs of \(f\) and \(g\) is revolved about the horizontal line \(y=2\).
\item[(c)] Let \(h\) be the function given by \(h(x)=k x(1-x)\) for \(0 \leq x \leq 1\). For each \(k>0\), the region (not shown) enclosed by the graphs of \(h\) and \(g\) is the base of a solid with square cross sections perpendicular to the \(x\)-axis. There is a value of \(k\) for which the volume of this solid is equal to 15 . Write, but do not solve, an equation involving an integral expression that could be used to find the value of \(k\).
\end{itemize}
![](https://cdn.mathpix.com/cropped/476aab1e-46ac-4e68-9b67-6944cf0a853a-1.jpg?height=496&width=395&top_left_y=367&top_left_x=1482)
\begin{itemize}
\item[(a)]
\[
\begin{aligned}
\text { Area } & =\int_{0}^{1}(f(x)-g(x)) d x \\
& =\int_{0}^{1}(2 x(1-x)-3(x-1) \sqrt{x}) d x=1.133
\end{aligned}
\]
\item[(b)]
\[
\begin{aligned}
& \text { Volume }=\pi \int_{0}^{1}\left((2-g(x))^{2}-(2-f(x))^{2}\right) d x \\
& =\pi \int_{0}^{1}\left((2-3(x-1) \sqrt{x})^{2}-(2-2 x(1-x))^{2}\right) d x \\
& =16.179
\end{aligned}
\]
\item[(c)]
\[
\begin{aligned}
& \text { Volume }=\int_{0}^{1}(h(x)-g(x))^{2} d x \\
& \int_{0}^{1}(k x(1-x)-3(x-1) \sqrt{x})^{2} d x=15
\end{aligned}
\]
\end{itemize}
